Track 2: Sulla’s Defiance
- Story & Context: Sulla, the monastery’s lead patch-operator, famously refused to clear the cache of the "Dream-Log" after a particularly violent night of tremors. She played a trumpet melody over the feedback, attempting to harmonize with the erratic blips of the machine while the other monks watched in terrified silence. "If the logic burns, let the melody catch," she shouted as the room filled with the scent of ozone and the sound of a thousand ticking clocks.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A woman with intense, piercing eyes standing in a dark room illuminated only by the frantic, multi-colored blinking LEDs of a massive wall of modular synthesizers, surreal vapor trails, dramatic shadows.

Track 3: Returned to Sender
- Story & Context: Years later, the letters sent to the monastery were found stacked in the courtyard, their stamps dated centuries into the future. Locals claim that if you put your ear to the cold stone at night, you can still hear the trumpet playing a final, distorted note that never actually ends. It is the sound of the myth closing, leaving only the "Silence arrives in a torn envelope" as a testament to the monks who transcribed the infinite.
